'''Monzen Town''' (門前町, monzen-machi) refers to a town formed around prominent {{ill|Buddhist temples|ja|寺院|12=draft}} or {{ill|Shinto shrines|ja|神社|12=draft}}. Specifically, for shrines, it is often called a '''Torii-mae Town''' (鳥居前町, torii-mae-machi).

== Overview ==
Broadly speaking, settlements formed by followers of temples or shrines, including {{ill|Shrines and Temples|ja|社家町|Shrines and Temples=Shrines and Temples|lt=shaji towns|12=draft}} and {{ill|Jinaimachi|ja|寺内町|fr|12=draft}}, are also considered Monzenmachi.<ref>
{{Cite web|和書|url=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E9%96%80%E5%89%8D%E7%94%BA-143199#E4.B8.96.E7.95.8C.E5.A4.A7.E7.99.BE.E7.A7.91.E4.BA.8B.E5.85.B8.20.E7.AC.AC.EF.BC.92.E7.89.88|title=Monzenmachi|publisher={{ill|World Encyclopedia|ja|世界大百科事典|12=draft}} 2nd Edition / Kotobank|accessdate=2018-03-07}}
</ref> Larger-scale examples may be defined as {{ill|Holy city|ja|宗教都市|lt=holy cities|12=draft}} or {{ill|Temple Precinct Cities|ja|境内都市|12=draft}}. Historically, sites for urban formation included castles, ports, markets, and exchange hubs, with temples and shrines being among these.

Monzen towns form when shrine or temple workers and merchants serving pilgrims gather in front of large shrines or temples attracting many visitors. However, the establishment of monzen towns is not guaranteed by the scale of the religious institution, as certain temples historically prohibited public access.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.worldtimes.co.jp/japan/20221119-166722/|title=70-Year-Old Thatch Roof Repair of Jionji Main Hall, a National Important Cultural Property in Yamagata Prefecture's Sagae City|publisher=The World Times|date=November 19, 2022|access-date=May 26, 2023}}</ref>

Regions that still retain historical elements as monzen towns are designated as {{ill|Important Preservation Districts for Groups of Traditional Buildings|ja|重要伝統的建造物群保存地区|12=draft}}, with preservation measures enacted. Since 1998, the {{ill|National Monzen Town Summit|ja|全国門前町サミット|12=draft}} has been held annually to promote exchanges between such towns.

== Monzen Towns and Torii-mae Towns in Important Preservation Districts ==

* [[Sakamoto (Ōtsu City)|Sakamoto]] - {{ill|Shiga Prefecture|ja|滋賀県|12=draft}}, {{ill|Ōtsu City|ja|大津市|12=draft}} - {{ill|Hiyoshi Taisha|ja|日吉大社|1=Hiyoshi Taisha|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Enryakuji|ja|延暦寺|12=draft}} (categorized as "Monzen Town and Sato-bo Group")
* [[Sagatoriimoto]] - {{ill|Kyoto Prefecture|ja|京都府|12=draft}}, {{ill|Kyoto City|ja|京都市|12=draft}}, {{ill|Ukyo Ward|ja|右京区|12=draft}} - {{ill|Atago Shrine|ja|愛宕神社|12=draft}}
* [[Sannenzaka]] - Kyoto City, {{ill|Higashiyama Ward|ja|東山区|12=draft}} - {{ill|Kiyomizu-dera|ja|清水寺|12=draft}}


== Important Monzenmachi and Toriimaemachi ==
